no relation between sites; tr is linear and cyclic, tr(X^dag) = conj tr(X), tr(I) = 1.
Normal form: E_{s,3} = I - E_{s,0} - E_{s,1} - E_{s,2} expanded at each site, adjacent
same-site products reduced, every trace written in cyclic words (lexicographically least
rotation), every real part split into the half-sum of a word and the word's adjoint.

Normal forms: C_ijk = Im z_ij + Im z_jk - Im z_ik has 18 cyclic words (length 2); P has 25, O has 24

